          a: 0,
          why: "Under 35, start with <b>ultrasound</b>: young breast tissue is too dense for mammography to work well, and the risk is too low to justify radiation. Over 35 it's a mammogram ± ultrasound; MRI is for a young woman at high risk. A lump that persists after a cycle gets investigated.",
