          a: 0,
          why: "Unilateral, single-duct, spontaneous, bloody discharge is <b>pathologic</b>: it comes from a lesion in the breast. The <b>commonest cause is a benign papilloma</b>; malignancy is only 5–10%. It still needs imaging, and papillomas are usually excised.",
