          a: 0,
          why: "Under 5 mm is reassuring for a <b>single</b> episode, but <b>recurrent bleeding with a thin endometrium still needs a biopsy</b>: not biopsying this group misses cancer 4% of the time. Type 2 cancers arise in an atrophic, thin endometrium.",
